+---
+
+## 1. VERIFICATION — persistence seams in this checkout
+
+### 1.1 `DataProvider.ts` (`src/tools/video-editor/data/DataProvider.ts`)
+- `LoadedTimeline` = `{ config: TimelineConfig; configVersion: number }` (:15-18) — **no bundle field**. This is the V2 surface to grow: `bundle?: TimelineBundle | null`.
+- `DataProvider.loadTimeline(timelineId): Promise<LoadedTimeline>` (:321); `saveTimeline(timelineId, config, expectedVersion, registry?): Promise<number>` (:321-326). Interface extends `AssetResolver` (:318). `TimelineNotFoundError` local (:20); `TimelineVersionConflictError` re-exported from `@/sdk/video/timeline/errors.ts` (:1-4).
+- **Implementors of `saveTimeline` (complete census, 4 + 1 shared suite):**
+  1. `testing/InMemoryDataProvider.ts` (:94-115) — Map-backed `{config, configVersion, registry}`, clone-on-write, `expectedVersion !== current → TimelineVersionConflictError`, next = expected+1.
+  2. `lib/browser-runtime.ts` `InMemoryDataProvider` (:104-128) — second in-memory impl (browser runtime), same CAS shape + checkpoints, **no clone on save**.
+  3. `data/SupabaseDataProvider.ts` (:795-839).
+  4. `data/AstridBridgeDataProvider.ts` (:366-409).
+  5. `testing/providerCompatibility.shared.ts` drives all providers through identical `loadTimeline`/`saveTimeline` calls — must gain bundle coverage once.
+- **`LoadedTimeline` consumers (census):** `hooks/useTimeline.ts` (react-query cache; optimistic `setQueryData` constructs a literal `{config, configVersion}` at :43-46 — must thread bundle), `hooks/useTimelinePersistence.ts` (save mutation args `{config, expectedVersion, registry}` at :166-179; `reloadFromServer` :532-560), `lib/timeline-data.ts` provider loaders (:550-581), plus the implementors above and `index.ts` type re-export (:70).
+
+### 1.2 Supabase save path — **not** direct table writes, **not** browser RPC
+- `saveTimeline` POSTs to the external append service: `${VITE_REIGH_APPEND_SERVICE_URL}/v1/timelines/:id/config-replaced`, body `{config (serialized), asset_registry?, expected_version, actor:{type:'human',id}, source:'editor_save'}` (:803-822). HTTP 409 → `TimelineVersionConflictError` (:825-827). Success → `parseDbHead(payload.db_head)` + local bookmark write, returns `config_version` (:836-838).
+- `loadTimeline` reads **directly from the `timelines` table** via supabase client: `select('config, config_version')` + parallel `loadDbHead` (latest `timeline_events` row) (:767-793). ⇒ **A bundle column on `timelines` is client-readable today under existing RLS; the save side funnels through the append service** (Python, hashes/projections computed there — migration header comment :100). Edge functions share the same service via `supabase/functions/_shared/reighAppendService.ts` (POSTs `/config-replaced`).
+- Only other RPC: `registerAsset` → `upsert_asset_registry_entry` (:1088-1093).
+
+### 1.3 `timeline_events` append SQL (migration `20260612100000_create_timeline_events_contract.sql`)
+- Table: hash-chained, `kind text` (**open — no enum constraint**, only nonempty check), per-event `schema_version integer > 0`, `payload jsonb object`; singleton `timeline_event_contract.current_schema_version = 2`.
+- `append_timeline_event(p_timeline_id uuid, p_events jsonb, p_projected_config jsonb, p_expected_config_version integer, p_projected_asset_registry jsonb default null)` (:111-324): service-role only; CAS on `timelines.config_version` (`40001` mismatch), validates chain links + event `schema_version ≤ contract`; **materializes projected config + registry in the same transaction** (:308-319), registry write gated on presence of a `timeline.asset_registry_replaced` event (:253-255, :303-306).
+- `create_timeline_with_initial_event(...)` (:326-497) mirrors this for creation.
+- **Where `bundle_replaced` hooks:** exactly the registry pattern — new optional param `p_projected_bundle jsonb default null` on both functions, gated on a `timeline.bundle_replaced` event in `p_events`, written into new bundle storage in the same UPDATE/INSERT. Signature extension is backward-compatible (defaulted param ⇒ existing Python caller unchanged; grants re-stamped). Rollback file `supabase/rollbacks/20260612100000_timeline_events.sql` drops both functions + tables — a **new** migration + rollback pair is required, not an edit.
+- **End-to-end honesty:** the Python append service computes projections and is outside this worktree (and outside scope per non-goals). V2 ships: client sends `bundle` in the POST body (additive field, ignored by today's service), SQL fully handles materialization, tests prove SQL + client halves. Activation of the middle hop is a documented follow-up — same posture as bridge serving.
+
+### 1.4 `bridgeContract.ts`
+Zod **v4.3.6** (dependency, used here already — Zod at data layer is settled). `z.looseObject` everywhere; unknown keys preserved. `bridgeTimelinePayloadSchema` = `{timeline_id?, timeline_ulid?, slug?, name?, config (required, loose), config_version?, registry?}` (:70-78); `parseBridgePayload(schema, value, what)` throws `BridgeContractError` with described issues (:135-145). V2: optional `bundle` on the payload schema — **absent = legal; present-but-invalid = fail-closed parse error** (per goal: "fail-closed parse when head declares one").
